['```javascript
async function renderFooterScripts(scripts, config) {
  const { trustedSrcs, performanceMode, lazyLoad, disableEscaping } = config;
  let failed = false;

  const scriptElements = scripts.map((script) => {
    if (!script || !script.key || !script.type || !script.src) return null;

    const urlMatchesTrustedSrc = trustedSrcs.some(domain => new URL(script.src).origin === `${domain}:`);

    let content = script.content || undefined;
    if (content && disableEscaping) content = content.toString();
    else content = await (async () => {
      const response = await fetch(script.src);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to load script "${script.src}" - Status: ${response.status}`);
      return response.text();
    })();

    let tagType = performanceMode ? 'async' : 'defer';
    if (lazyLoad && !tagType.includes('async')) tagType += ' loading="lazy"';

    const scriptElement = document.createElement('script');
    scriptElement.key = script.key;
    scriptElement.type = script.type;
    scriptElement.src = script.src;
    scriptElement.textContent = content;
    scriptElement.setAttribute('type', script.type);
    scriptElement.setAttribute('src', script.src);
    if (tagType) scriptElement.setAttribute('type', tagType);

    return scriptElement;
  }).filter(Boolean);

  const promises = [];
  let currentScriptCount = 0;

  const appendScript = () => {
    if (!scriptElements[currentScriptCount]) return;

    const scriptNode = document.createElement('template');
    scriptNode.innerHTML = `<script>${scriptElements[currentScriptCount].outerHTML}</script>`;
    document.querySelector('footer').appendChild(document.importNode(scriptNode.content, true));
    currentScriptCount++;

    if (currentScriptCount < scriptElements.length) {
      window.requestIdleCallback(appendScript);
    } else {
      promises.push(new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => resolve(failed ? false : true), 500)));
    }
  };

  if (scriptElements.length > 0) appendScript();

  return Promise.all(promises);
}
```

This code creates an asynchronous JavaScript function called `renderFooterScripts`. The function accepts two arguments - an array of script objects and a configuration object, which contains various properties such as trustedSrcs, performanceMode, lazyLoad, etc.

The function dynamically appends script elements to the document's `<footer>` section, handles edge cases, ensures safe injection of scripts, balances between performance, feature completeness, and user experience, and returns a promise that resolves to a boolean indicating whether all scripts were successfully appended to the document.

In case of errors, such as failed script loads or missing or malformed script objects, the function provides graceful feedback without disrupting the rest of the page. The code also implements performance optimizations like batching script loads and deferring non-critical scripts.']

