[' Here's a PHP implementation of the `DataHandler` class:

```php
<?php

namespace App;

use RuntimeException;
use SplObjectStorage;
use function hash_hmac;
use function openssl_random_pseudo_bytes;

class DataHandler
{
    private const CHARSET = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';

    /** @var SplObjectStorage Store for unique identifiers */
    private $identifiers;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this->identifiers = new SplObjectStorage();
    }

    public function generateUniqueIdentifier($length, $charset = self::CHARSET)
    {
        do {
            $candidate = '';
            for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
                $candidate .= $charset[mt_rand(0, strlen($charset) - 1)];
            }
        } while (!$this->identifiers->contains($candidate));

        $this->identifiers[$candidate] = true;

        return $candidate;
    }

    public function securelyHashData($data)
    {
        return hash_hmac('sha256', $data, openssl_random_pseudo_bytes(32));
    }

    /**
     * AsyncReadFile using a promise-based approach
     */
    public function asyncReadFile($filePath)
    {
        if (!file_exists($filePath)) {
            throw new RuntimeException("File '$filePath' does not exist.");
        }

        $promise = new \SplPromise(function (callable $resolve, callable $reject) use ($filePath) {
            $handle = fopen($filePath, 'r');
            if (!$handle) {
                $reason = error_get_last()['message'];
                $reject(new RuntimeException("Error opening file '$filePath': $reason"));
                return;
            }

            $content = '';
            while (!feof($handle)) {
                $content .= fgets($handle);
            }

            fclose($handle);
            if ($content === '') {
                throw new RuntimeException("File '$filePath' is empty.");
            }

            $resolve($content);
        });

        return $promise->then(function ($value) {
            return (string)$value;
        })->onRejected(function (\Throwable $reason) {
            throw $reason;
        });
    }
}
```

In this PHP implementation, we use an `SplObjectStorage` for managing unique identifiers and a custom promise-based approach to handle asynchronous file reading. The class is modular, handles different data sources, supports various file types, and ensures efficient resource management.

