Regarding resource management, memory usage can be minimized by using VecDeque instead of Vec when dealing with token streams, since it allows efficient removal of elements from either end without reallocating the entire buffer. Performance optimization can be achieved through concurrent execution (using rayon or similar libraries) and careful handling of system dependencies.

In terms of trade-offs:

- Efficiency vs. usability: The use of incremental parsing enhances reliability and user experience, but it may come at the cost of increased complexity and longer startup times.
- Maintainability vs. scalability: Integrating external grammar definitions dynamically without recompilation can improve maintainability, but it may make the codebase more complex and harder to understand for new developers.
