In case of excessive memory consumption, the function removes the oldest entries when the limit is approached. The trade-off between using a fixed-size buffer and a variable-size buffer is addressed by using a dynamically resizing doubly linked list, which allows for efficient handling of large-scale data while minimizing memory overhead and fragmentation.

